  "notes": "Milestone 1 and chat editing have offline and live evidence. The itinerary now keeps source-attributed photos and omits the route map at the user's request. The Streamlit and JavaScript graph pages display the compiled LangGraph PNG returned by get_graph_image() inside responsive panels, with SVG fallback; JavaScript image delivery has host-test evidence. Vietnamese is the default webapp chat language. Coordinator routes work, Planner owns search/proposals, and Chat writes responses. Committed Chat replies receive the Planner summary and validated plan; rejected replies receive validation issues and the retained prior plan without the rejected candidate. The JavaScript chat composer is a lower-right floating panel with accessible focus/close behavior and separate right/left user and assistant conversation bubbles. The interface now uses a blue and near-black visual system; frontend check/build pass while browser QA remains pending. Trip extension resolves the requested total before Planner and rejects invalid bounds before search. Planner model output excludes provider-owned returned-source inventory; grounding attaches trusted sources after structured parsing. Tavily prompt snippets remain capped at 1,000 characters and grounded source references allow 4,000. Coordinator defaults to gpt-5.5 while Planner and Chat default to gpt-5.4-mini; no new live provider run is claimed for the model split, extension flow or Chat context fix. Source-quality metrics still have a synthetic baseline and live relevance remains unmeasured. Old POC counts are archived. The JavaScript/Tailwind UI is now the current container frontend; browser QA is pending."
